{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"694c391740c88ca14657e9ea3ebe630027570b9054985aeb9e17a5e35544a972","digest":{"component_or_area":"fallback-endpoint test","key_entities":["tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py","test_a_fallback_entry_endpoint_is_built_against_that_endpoint","_FALLBACK_ENDPOINT","_origin","urllib.parse.urlsplit","model.models[1].base_url","model.models[0].base_url"],"problem_keywords":["URL validation","incomplete substring sanitization","security","CodeQL","test assertion"],"propositions":["The test uses `startswith` to check URL prefixes, which permits suffix-sharing look-alike hosts like `https://fallback.test.evil.example/` to pass validation.","Assertions at lines 249 and 250 in `test_llm_fallback_chain.py` trigger CodeQL alerts `py/incomplete-url-substring-sanitization` because prefix matching is weaker than host validation.","URL origin comparison via `urllib.parse.urlsplit` extracting `(scheme, netloc)` and comparing by exact equality eliminates both the CodeQL alert and the weak assertion pattern.","The test must continue to fail if the fallback entry is built against the provider default instead of the configured endpoint, preserving the property the test protects."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787730296999911001,"uuid":"9f08a8bc-d66a-4534-b17a-55f1c643a00e"}